Explicit path/class licence map
-------------------------------

`REUSE.toml` is the machine-readable, authoritative map. In summary:

  * Imported or executable schemas are Apache-2.0 code, alongside Python source,
    tests, tools, CI/configuration, and schemas under `src/`;
  * synthetic operation fixtures and scenario definitions under `examples/`,
    documentation under `docs/`, and project prose are under CC-BY-4.0;
  * canonical licence texts under `LICENSES/` state their own licences.

A file has one licence under this map. There is no mixed-use fallback. A schema
that is imported, validated, or otherwise executed by the package is
Apache-2.0 code even when its syntax is JSON or YAML.

Attribution
-----------

Attribution should name the project, the version or commit used, and link to the
repository. For example:

    OperateBench (https://github.com/DwellyOrg/OperateBench), operation
    fixture <operation_id> v<operation_version>, licensed under CC BY 4.0.

For results from this preview, state the operation version and spec digest, the
unified engine version, artifact version, scenario/variant ids and the run's state
and trajectory digests. Separate runtime/evaluator versions and bundle digests
are target-design fields that this build does not emit. See docs/VERSIONING.md.

